<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Allen Code Co — sitemap.xml

  Lives at https://www.allencodeco.com/sitemap.xml and is referenced from
  /robots.txt.

  ROUTES LISTED (as of 2026-08-24)
    src/App.jsx used to mount the app inside a <HashRouter>, which made
    every route below the homepage a URL fragment (/#/products, and so
    on) — invisible to crawlers, since everything after '#' is dropped
    before the request is ever made and Google retired the AJAX-crawling
    scheme that used to work around that.

    That's fixed: App.jsx uses the browser router, and every path below is
    built as its own HTML file (Phase 9, 2026-11-10: tools/prerender), so
    a direct hit serves that page; vercel.json rewrites any other path
    (except /api/*, which stays routed to the serverless functions) to the
    shell, spa.html. Every real route is a genuine, separately fetchable
    URL, so all of them are listed here.

    Deliberately NOT listed: /checkout-success (post-purchase
    transactional page, not something search should surface) and the
    catch-all 404 route.

  PER-PAGE HTML (was KNOWN LIMITATION — SOCIAL PREVIEW CRAWLERS)
    `npm run build` prerenders every <loc> below into its own HTML file
    with that page's own title, description, canonical, Open Graph and
    Twitter tags and its real content (Phase 9). Link-preview bots
    (Facebook, LinkedIn, X, Slack) and crawlers that do not run JavaScript
    now read each page's own tags. A path added here is prerendered on the
    next build; it must be a real route that answers 200, or the build
    fails naming it.

  NAMESPACE
    Correct sitemaps.org namespace (singular "sitemap" in the old xmlns
    value would fail Search Console validation).

  LAST MODIFIED
    Update <lastmod> on a given <url> whenever that page's content is
    materially edited, so re-crawling is prioritized correctly.
-->
